        "original_id": "30c2e469-2111-5dcd-8cda-e5155689bf50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred Döblin, César Vallejo\n- Works: Berlin Alexanderplatz, Tales of a Long Night\n- Topics: literature, authors\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred Döblin was born on 10 August 1878 and died on 26 June 1957.\n- Alfred Döblin was a German novelist, essayist, and doctor.\n- César Vallejo was born on March 16, 1892 and died on April 15, 1938.\n- César Vallejo was a Peruvian poet, writer, playwright, and journalist.\n- Alfred Döblin is best known for the 1929 novel Berlin Alexanderplatz.\n- Tales of a Long Night, titled Hamlet oder Die lange Nacht nimmt ein Ende in German, was published in 1956.\n- Tales of a Long Night was the last novel by German author Alfred Döblin.",
